                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Health Services Management is a discipline that studies the patterns of development in the health sector and macro-level health development planning. It aims to seek optimal health services, scientifically and rationally allocate and utilize health resources, and to the greatest extent, meet people's needs for medical, preventive, and healthcare services. This course primarily includes the following content: (1) the purpose and operational principles of the health sector; (2) structure: organizational systems, resource allocation (human, financing, material, and information), and management mechanisms; (3) process: management of service processes; (4) outcomes: system outcomes and their evaluation; (5) the impact of the external environment: politics/economy/culture/biology/environment/behavior.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
